{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261124T160554Z-0c61c80e", "ts": "2026-11-24T16:08:38Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "fix/credential-placeholders", "build": "391e202c37c3"}, "body": {"base_commit": "391e202c37c3f25ab208a1fd34bd31b73bb72c17", "base_tree": "240ec26ca8c7be496cbb4e1d25ced9acb634d4e3", "head_tree": "6815d26029e0542df191a5fe8cd06fba1c05c729", "head_commit": "9beca39ec5c48ee4f4d311314061bd48f018d324", "dispatch_commit": "9beca39ec5c48ee4f4d311314061bd48f018d324", "mode": "final (full review, ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "fallback-no-prior-findings", "stage": "inner", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py", "tests/test_pr_gate.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py", "tests/test_pr_gate.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "branch_credential_shapes' own unchecked paths are never exercised: only the caller's handling of them is", "recommendation": "Instance. The new public entry point has three ways to answer 'unchecked': an unresolvable base branch, no merge-base, and an exception from the check. Every test that reaches begin_review's unchecked branch monkeypatches branch_credential_shapes to return a canned tuple, and no test calls the real function on a repo without a resolvable base, or with _credential_shape raising. So nothing pins that a failure to look comes back as ([], reason) and not as a clean ([], None), which is the distinction its docstring says the caller rules on. Add one test on a repo with no resolvable base branch and one with _credential_shape patched to raise, each asserting a non-None second element. At inner stage this is an error-path coverage rating, not a finding.", "files": ["plugin/lib/pr_gate.py", "tests/test_critic_dispatch_credential_shape.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "The second-@ guard stops at the first '/', so 'a password holding an unencoded @ still refuses' does not hold when it also holds a '/'", "recommendation": "Instance. _URL_AUTHORITY is `://[^/\\s]*`, so for `https://admin:ab@Xk9/mQ@host` the authority is `://admin:ab@Xk9`, which has one '@'. The password is then judged as `ab` (three characters or fewer) and exempted. Before this change the base regex reported it. That case is contrived (an unencoded '@' and '/' in one raw password) and the PR gate's backstop is otherwise intact, but the sentence in plugin/docs/waivers.md is stated without that bound. Either count '@' up to the host's terminator rather than the first '/', or bound the doc claim. Not exploitable as written, so not a security finding.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py", "plugin/docs/waivers.md"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "A per-shape exception is special-cased by name inside the table-driven loop", "recommendation": "`credential_shape` now walks `_SECRET_SHAPES` and then branches on `name == _URL_PASSWORD` to apply `_has_real_url_password`. The table already holds per-shape behaviour (`line_form`, `is_credential`), so the placeholder filter could be one more column, an optional `(line) -> bool` predicate, and the loop would stay uniform. Today this is a single shape, so no change is needed. Make it a column the next time a shape gains its own exemption, so the loop does not collect name checks.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "pr_gate and critic_consolidate now import each other", "recommendation": "`pr_gate` already imports `critic_consolidate` lazily, for `TREE_CHANGED_KEY` and `describe_tree_change`. `begin_review` now imports `pr_gate` lazily for `branch_credential_shapes`. Both imports are function-local, so nothing breaks today. Still, the two modules now depend on each other, and a future module-level import in either one would create an import cycle. No edit is wanted. If either import ever needs to move to module level, move `branch_credential_shapes` (or the tree-change helpers) into a leaf module both can import.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The second-@ authority read runs past the host into the query string", "recommendation": "`_URL_AUTHORITY = re.compile(r\"://[^/\\s]*\")` stops only at `/` or whitespace. On a URL with no path, such as `postgres://app:password@db?user=a@b`, it reads `?user=a@b` as part of the authority, finds two `@`, and reports the placeholder password as real. The PR gate and the cumulative guard share this code, so the two agree, and a waiver clears the line. The cost is an occasional false refusal, not a missed secret. Instance fix: add `?#` to the excluded set, `[^/?#\\s]*`, which is where RFC 3986 says the authority ends. Correctness owns whether this needs a test.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "cmd_critic_begin's exit-code docstring enumerates exits 2-8 and 'exit 1 = any other' but not the new exit 9", "recommendation": "Instance. The docstring of `cmd_critic_begin` in plugin/bin/prawduct-hook lists every critic-begin sentinel exit individually (2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, then 'exit 1 = any other dispatch failure'). This change added exit 9 to the handler, SKILL.md and api-contract.md \u00a7 Error Model, but not to this list. A maintainer reading the CLI's own enumeration would conclude 9 is not a code critic-begin returns. It is wording, rated an observation. A fix is one clause beside exit 8, or making the list relational ('the sentinels in api-contract.md \u00a7 Error Model') so the next sentinel cannot leave it behind.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "The exemption set's survey figure (176 of 204 exempt) predates the single-case-name tightening, and nothing can re-derive it", "recommendation": "The plan's Goals cite a 2026-11-24 survey (204 matches, 176 exempt, all placeholders) as the reason for the exemption set. Its 'Decisions made mid-build' entry then narrows template content to a single-case name (`_NAME` in plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py: `[a-z_][a-z0-9_.]*` or the upper-case form). That change now refuses camelCase and hyphenated placeholders such as `{dbPassword}`, `${dbPass}` and `<your-password>`, which are common in docs, and the record does not say whether the survey was re-run afterwards. The decision's recorded why may therefore rest on a measurement of a different rule. The learnings rule applies: 'A spike that discards its code leaves its numbers unfalsifiable \u2014 commit the derivation as a runnable script and cite the COMMAND'. Re-measuring under the shipped rule, and citing the command that does it, would show whether hyphenated and camelCase names belong in `_NAME`. Today a consumer writing them needs a waiver, which is the reflex-waiver cost this change set out to remove.", "files": ["plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Records Pass: covered all five oracle files; none clears a bar", "recommendation": "Covered: .prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md, .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md, .prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md, .prawduct/changes/credential-placeholders.md, .prawduct/owner-rulings.md. Checked against the code: the `--force` override list (3, 4, 7, 9 and correctly not 8, whose refusal has no force branch), the guard-refusal body (`mode`/`branch`/`lines`, reason `credential-shape`, lines never recorded), 'refused before anything is derived', the `--mode cumulative` flag, the exemption families including `%(name)s` and `{{ name }}`, the balanced-wrapper and second-`@` rules, and the `--force` note naming the skipped lines. All hold. No record ships a false claim or misleads into action. No edit is wanted.", "oid": "O-8"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "credential-placeholders", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": "240ec26ca8c7be496cbb4e1d25ced9acb634d4e3", "chunks": ["01", "02"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02"], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {"01": {"paths": ["plugin/docs/waivers.md", "plugin/lib/backlog/transport.py"], "paths_more": 0, "commits": ["d2acd17485b2"]}, "02": {"paths": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/pr_gate.py"], "paths_more": 1, "commits": ["538076851900"]}}, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-credential-placeholders.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/crede